1️⃣ What does DOM mean (in general)?
DOM = Document Object Model

Simple definition
The DOM is a tree-like representation of your HTML page, created by the browser, so that JavaScript can read, change, add, or remove elements.

Example HTML
<html>
  <body>
    <h1>Hello</h1>
    <p>Welcome</p>
  </body>
</html>
How the browser sees it (DOM Tree)
Document
 └── html
     └── body
         ├── h1 → "Hello"
         └── p  → "Welcome"
Each tag becomes an object (node) in the DOM.

Why DOM exists?
HTML alone is static.
DOM makes it dynamic.

Example:

document.querySelector("h1").innerText = "Hi";
👉 JavaScript talks to the DOM, not directly to HTML.

Key point (General DOM)
Created by the browser

Represents the real page

JavaScript uses it to update UI

Slow if updated too often

2️⃣ What is DOM in React?
React does NOT work directly with the real DOM for every change.

Instead, it uses something called the Virtual DOM.

3️⃣ What is Virtual DOM (React)?
Simple meaning
The Virtual DOM is a lightweight copy of the real DOM, kept in memory by React.

