🔹 What are Lifecycle Methods?
👉 Lifecycle methods are special functions that run at different stages of a component’s life.

A component’s life has steps, just like a person.

🧠 One-line meaning
Lifecycle methods let React run code when a component is created, updated, or removed.

🔁 Component Life Stages (Very Simple)
1️⃣ Birth → Mounting
Component appears on screen

2️⃣ Change → Updating
Component data changes

3️⃣ Death → Unmounting
Component disappears from screen

🔧 Lifecycle Methods (Easy Examples)
Stage	Method	What it does
Mount	componentDidMount	Runs after component appears
Update	componentDidUpdate	Runs after component updates
Unmount	componentWillUnmount	Runs before component is removed
🧠 Why lifecycle methods are needed?
To:

Fetch data

Set timers

Clean up memory

Handle errors

🚨 Lifecycle methods for Errors
Special ones:

getDerivedStateFromError

componentDidCatch

👉 Used to catch UI crashes and show fallback UI

🧠 Real-life analogy
Lifecycle methods are like:

Birth certificate

Health checkups

Death certificate

🧾 Interview-ready answer
Lifecycle methods are special React class component methods that run at different stages of a component’s life, such as mounting, updating, and unmounting.

🧠 Super short summary
Lifecycle methods = component life steps

Used in class components

Hooks replaced most of them

